\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Korea hogs limelight, Wall St takes supporting role. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Nick Edwards \par \uc2 1,154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2001\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, Nov 14 (Reuters) - South Korean assets held \par \par \uc2  centre stage in Asia for a second day on Wednesday, riding the \par \par \uc2  wave of an upgrade and a tech stock rally that pushed shares to \par \par \uc2  near five month highs and domestic bond yields to two month \par \par \uc2  lows. \par \par \uc2      A Wall Street rally, prompted by hopes for a swift end to \par \par \uc2  the war in Afghanistan after a series of opposition victories \par \par \uc2  against the Taliban, lent additional support to Seoul and \par \par \uc2  underpinned stock surges in Japan, Hong Kong and Taiwan. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors bought a net 152 billion won ($118.9 \par \par \uc2  million) worth of Korean stocks, reversing their position on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday as net sellers, while domestic liquidity drove a second \par \par \uc2  leg of a rally in U.S. dollar denominated Korean bonds. \par \par \uc2      "We like a lot of the stories up there," Jason Carley, head \par \par \uc2  of Asian fixed income research at Merrill Lynch in Hong Kong, \par \par \uc2  told Reuters. \par \par \uc2      Korean sovereign paper due 2008 rallied six basis points \par \par \uc2  (bps), taking them to 122 bps tighter for the year so far and \par \par \uc2  making them Asia's best performing high grade sovereign. \par \par \uc2      Global ratings agency Standard & Poor's on Tuesday raised \par \par \uc2  Korea's long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating by one notch to \par \par \uc2  BBB-plus from BBB, citing steady progress in structural reform, \par \par \uc2  fiscal flexibility and a strong external position. \par \par \uc2      Korean onshore investors are big buyers of the nation's \par \par \uc2  dollar debt, attracted by its higher yield and the security of \par \par \uc2  the greenback. \par \par \uc2      "Top tier, high grade Asia will remain very strongly \par \par \uc2  supported for the next six months," Carley said. \par \par \uc2      Korea's rally supported a broad spread tightening across \par \par \uc2  the Asian dollar bond market. \par \par \uc2      WALL STREET LIFTS ASIA \par \par \uc2      Tokyo stocks snapped a three-day losing streak, but gains \par \par \uc2  were substantially smaller than those in the U.S. and major \par \par \uc2  indices gave up much of their early gains as bleak domestic \par \par \uc2  factors, bad-loan problems in particular, reasserted \par \par \uc2  themselves. \par \par \uc2      The benchmark Nikkei average ended up 0.56 percent while \par \par \uc2  the capital-weighted TOPIX index rose 0.26 percent. \par \par \uc2      A 3.4-percent hike on Taiwan's TAIEX was the biggest move \par \par \uc2  on a benchmark index in Asia on the day. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors were net buyers of T$7.9 billion (US$229 \par \par \uc2  million) worth of Taiwan shares after buying a net T$591 \par \par \uc2  million in the previous session, as the TAIEX rose to its \par \par \uc2  highest close since September 11. \par \par \uc2  Gains on the U.S. Nasdaq and the Philadelphia semiconductor \par \par \uc2  index spurred buying in Taipei's heavily-weighted electronics \par \par \uc2  sector where the electronics sub-index shot up 4.79 percent. \par \par \uc2      Hong Kong blue chips ended sharply higher too, with the \par \par \uc2  Hang Seng Index ending up 2.7 percent at a five-month high. \par \par \uc2      Some investors were optimistic ahead of the release of U.S. \par \par \uc2  October retail sales data due later on Wednesday. Analysts in a \par \par \uc2  Reuters poll forecast a 2.7-percent rise. \par \par \uc2      Any upswing in U.S. consumer confidence was likely to add \par \par \uc2  impetus to a long-awaited liquidity-driven equity rally, Robert \par \par \uc2  Rountree, head of Asian strategy at Prudential-Bache Securities \par \par \uc2  in Hong Kong, told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2      But that would only be a short-term phenomenon, he \par \par \uc2  cautioned. \par \par \uc2      "We should see quite strongly liquidity-driven markets \par \par \uc2  before people get that out of the way and say 'Well what's \par \par \uc2  happening longer term?' because longer term there's quite a \par \par \uc2  different picture emerging," Rountree said. \par \par \uc2  "People are going to ask the question of should they price \par \par \uc2  equities at the same level on 12-percent earnings growth as \par \par \uc2  they have for the past 10 years on 15-percent growth? The \par \par \uc2  answer, I suspect, is going to be no," he said. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR BUCKS SOFTER TREND \par \par \uc2  The stock market surge helped lift the Taiwan dollar to \par \par \uc2  four-month highs against the dollar, closing at T$34.499 after \par \par \uc2  opening weaker at an intraday low of T$34.520. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's close was the highest since July 6 and \par \par \uc2  contrasted with an otherwise limp performance by Asian \par \par \uc2  regionals as the dollar was boosted by hopes of a speedy end to \par \par \uc2  the Afghan conflict and fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  News that the U.S.-supported Northern Alliance had captured \par \par \uc2  the Afghan capital of Kabul from the ruling Taliban spurred the \par \par \uc2  greenback to three-month highs against the euro and pushed it \par \par \uc2  through resistance of 121.30 against the yen. \par \par \uc2  In Tokyo trade, the dollar climbed to a fresh one-week high \par \par \uc2  against the yen at 121.80 yen, but later slipped back to be bid \par \par \uc2  at around 121.55 in late Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  Trading in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was thinned by a market \par \par \uc2  holiday in Singapore. Financial markets in the city state will \par \par \uc2  reopen on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      The Philippine peso crawled off its intraday low of 52.18 \par \par \uc2  to the dollar, thanks to rumoured \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      Dealers in Manila said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have sold \par \par \uc2  around $10-$20 million to defend the peso below 52.10. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. $0943 GMT \par \par \uc2  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.85       121.24         -0.50\par  Sing dlr      1.8259       1.8250         -0.05\par  Taiwan dlr     34.45        34.46         +0.03\par  Korean won   1282.00      1273.00         -0.70\par  Baht           44.38        44.42         +0.09\par  Peso           52.09        52.07         -0.04\par  Rupiah      10630.00     10670.00         +0.38\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.85       114.45         -6.07\par  Sing dlr      1.8259       1.7365         -4.90\par  Taiwan dlr     34.45        32.90         -4.50\par  Korean won   1282.00      1277.00         -0.39\par  Baht           44.38        43.70         -1.53\par  Peso           52.09        50.75         -2.57\par  Rupiah      10630.00      9470.00        -10.91\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7997         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ------------------------------------------------\par \f2