\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar extends gains as Taliban retreat. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Robin Shepherd \par \uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2001\par 14:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 13 (Reuters) - The dollar hit two month highs against the euro on Tuesday as U.S. backed Afghan opposition fighters advanced on the Taliban stronghold of Kandahar, having earlier taken the capital, Kabul. \par \par \uc2  Since fears over the efficacy and potential duration of the U.S. bombing campaign had previously weighed upon the dollar, dealers and analysts said the reports of major victories were bound to be positive for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar began its upward surge in Asia as initial investigations suggested Monday's New York plane crash was an accident and not a follow-up to the September 11 attacks. But in late European morning trade, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were awash with talk of Afghanistan. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is strengthening today because the Taliban is on the run," said Jesper Dannesboe, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein in London. "This is the key driver behind \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets." \par \par \uc2  The dollar posted its biggest one day gains in weeks. It rose one percent against the euro to hit an intra day high of $0.8838. Against the Swiss franc it was up by more than one percent at 1.6369, a two week high. And against the yen the dollar was up two thirds of a percent at 121.19. \par \par \uc2  The pound also took heart from dollar strength, hitting a 10 week high against the euro beyond 61.13 pence. \par \par \uc2  AFGHAN VICTORIES SPUR DOLLAR BULLS \par \par \uc2  U.S.-backed anti-Taliban fighters entered the Afghan capital Kabul on Tuesday as reports from across the country pointed to a collapse of Taliban rule. \par \par \uc2  Combined with a reversal of the flight from the dollar immediately after Monday's plane crash, this made the greenback an irresistible bet for many. \par \par \uc2  "Easing security fears and the potentially brighter picture in Afghanistan have got the dollar bulls back on the road," said a trader at a British bank. \par \par \uc2  He added that the euro's break of key chart support at $0.8845 had darkened the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's outlook from a technical point of view. \par \par \uc2  On the macro-economic front, the dollar's rise against the euro was helped by disappointing French inflation data. French consumer prices unexpectedly rose in October, denting the prospect of further growth-boosting interest rate cuts from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's threat to resign and break up the ruling coalition if it did not back him in a vote on troop mobilisation for Afghanistan was also weighing on euro sentiment. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN KNOCKS YEN \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rally against the yen was further aided when Japan's senior finance ministry official, Zembei Mizoguchi, reiterated that the government stood ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap yen strength. \par \par \uc2  Talk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Furukawa Electric Co Ltd was buying dollars to complete its purchase of a U.S. optical unit from Lucent Technologies Inc also swirled through trading floors. \par \par \uc2  The original $2.75 billion deal has been delayed twice and Furukawa faces a deadline of November 16 to settle. \par \par \uc2  Indications of a strong opening on Wall Street were also helping the dollar. The Nasdaq December future was up by almost two percent at 1,558. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba000002001111