\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar gains ground against yen on Japan warning. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 677 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2001\par 14:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The dollar chalked up modest gains against the yen on Monday after a clear reminder from a top Japanese official that monetary authorities remained ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent any significant yen appreciation. \par \par \uc2  The euro edged down against the Swiss franc and the dollar on mildly negative sentiment following last week's surprise European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cut but, overall, trading was subdued as U.S. markets pause for a national holiday. \par \par \uc2  The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings out of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  came from the country's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda who told Reuters during a visit to Australia that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if exchange rates "deviated from fundamentals". \par \par \uc2  "The dollar should be well supported this week with expectations of better U.S. data and a warning from Japanese policymakers that they don't want to see the yen rise," said Razia Khan, treasury economist at Standard Chartered Bank. \par \par \uc2  In the absence of any major data on Monday, investors were awaiting the release of U.S. retail sales and industrial production figures later in the week. \par \par \uc2  By 1300 GMT, the dollar was stuck near 120.69 yen, pulling itself off from its one-month low of 119.75 hit last week. \par \par \uc2  The euro was down around a quarter of a percent against the dollar at $0.8920 and hit a seven week low against the Swiss franc of 1.4628. \par \par \uc2  "The Swiss National Bank's decision to leave rates unchanged is one of the supporting factors because rate differentials favour the franc," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the Swiss National Bank left its main interest rates unchanged while the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut by 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  The euro failed to draw support from comments by European Commission spokesman Gerassimos Thomas that the euro was still undervalued and does not accurately reflect euro zone economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  MORE U.S. DATA \par \par \uc2  Analysts polled by Reuters expect U.S. retail sales, due on Wednesday, to rise 2.7 percent in October, fully reversing the 2.4 percent drop in September which was the sharpest drop in nine years. \par \par \uc2  They expected a firmer retail sales figure would likely boost market faith in the U.S. recovery scenario supporting both asset markets and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  U.S. October industrial production is due on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Chief White House economic adviser Glenn Hubbard said the U.S. economy is likely to show a relatively weak start to the forth quarter but that it should recover in the first quarter of next year. \par \par \uc2  He said his forecasts for economic performance in the coming quarters depended in part on approval in Congress of a stimulus package in the coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market would also be on the lookout for policy clues from Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan, who speaks on Tuesday and Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  They added \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were not noticeably affected by news anti-Taliban forces took key strategic towns in the north of the country over the weekend. \par \par \uc2  LIMITED SCOPE FOR YEN RISE \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were taking threats of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seriously because of repeated bouts of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, in which it used more than $27 billion to halt the yen rise. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government is concerned an already weak economy could be hit further if a strengthening yen were to damage export prospects. \par \par \uc2  A Bank of Japan survey showed nearly three in four Japanese consumers think the economy is worsening but an increasing proportion feel that a slowdown is an acceptable price for structural reform. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan starts its two-day policy board meeting on Thursday but is expected to leave policy unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Latest data from the Chicago Mercantile Exchange showed yen short positions held by speculators fell to their smallest in three weeks, limiting scope for further yen rises. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also said speculators still held large net euro long positions against the dollar, which pointed to the downside risk for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011112dxbc00pxg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
