\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar pushes up against yen with Japan warning. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2001\par 11:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The dollar chalked up modest gains against the yen on Monday after a clear reminder from a top Japanese official that monetary authorities remained ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent any significant yen appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Trading was largely subdued as U.S. markets pause for a national day holiday, with investors eyeing another run of key U.S. data due later this week. \par \par \uc2  The latest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  warnings out of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  came from the country's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda who told Reuters during a visit to Australia that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if exchange rates "deviated from fundamentals". \par \par \uc2  "We had a clear indication that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is pretty much out there watching the market, that is supporting the dollar," Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers said. \par \par \uc2  The market was focused on U.S. October retail sales due on Wednesday and October industrial production on Friday for more clues about the state of the world's biggest economy. \par \par \uc2  "Worse-than-expected U.S. data could again hurt the dollar against the yen and the euro, but the dollar is unlikely to go significantly lower against the yen." \par \par \uc2  By 1040 GMT, the dollar nudged higher nearly half a yen to 120.83 at one stage, pulling itself off from its one-month low of 119.75 hit last week. \par \par \uc2  The greenback ticked up against the euro to $0.8928 from $0.8940 in late New York on Friday. The euro was nearly unchanged against the yen at 107.62. \par \par \uc2  LIMITED SCOPE FOR YEN RISE \par \par \uc2  Analysts said \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were taking threats of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seriously because of repeated bouts of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September, in which it used more than $27 billion to halt the yen rise. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government is concerned that an already weak economy could be hit further if a strengthening yen were to damage export prospects. \par \par \uc2  A Bank of Japan survey showed nearly three in four Japanese consumers think the economy is worsening but an increasing proportion feel that a slowdown is an acceptable price for structural reform. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan starts its two-day policy board meeting on Thursday but is expected to leave policy unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Latest data from the Chicago Mercantile Exchange showed yen short positions held by speculators fell to their smallest in three weeks, limiting scope for further yen rises. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also said speculators still held large net euro long positions against the dollar, which pointed to the downside risk for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The main driving force for this week will be again how speculators are positioned," said Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merril Lynch. \par \par \uc2  MORE U.S. DATA \par \par \uc2  Analysts polled by Reuters expect U.S. retail sales to rise 2.7 percent in October, fully reversing the 2.4 percent drop in September which was the sharpest drop in nine years. \par \par \uc2  They expected a firmer retail sales figure would likely boost market faith in the US recovery scenario supporting both asset markets and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Chief White House economic adviser Glenn Hubbard said the U.S. economy is likely to show a relatively weak start to the forth quarter but that it should recover in the first quarter of next year. \par \par \uc2  He said his forecasts for economic performance in the coming quarters depended in part on approval in Congress of a stimlus package in the coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  Dealers added \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were not noticably affected by news anti-Taliban forces took key strategic towns in the north of the country over the weekend. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011112dxbc00lb5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
