\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 - \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  wariness curbs yen, euro limps. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 729 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2001\par 14:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 9 (Reuters) - The yen retreated from this week's one-month highs against the dollar on Friday on wariness about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap its strength, while the euro stayed weak after a half-point cut in euro-zone rates on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda said in Tokyo that recent yen moves were unfavourable, reminding the market of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's aggressive yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, failed to convince the market it was tackling the euro zone's economic problems with the same gusto applied to the U.S. economy by the Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is quite likely should the yen strengthen further," said Teis Knuthsen, chief strategist at SEB Merchant Banking in Copenhagen. \par \par \uc2  "Policy-makers in the United States have accepted there is going to be a recession and they have acted aggressively, but in the euro zone nobody is willing or able to take responsibility for the economy," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 120.30 yen at 1250 GMT, more than half a yen above one-month lows set in the previous session. \par \par \uc2  The euro hovered above $0.89 , after hitting two-week lows of $0.8889 in Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its poise against the yen, however, trading around half a yen above six-week lows of 106.76 set on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Bank of France Governor Jean-Claude Trichet said in the European session that the ECB's 50 basis point rate cut on Thursday to 3.25 percent was a sign of confidence, and also that it was vital the 12 nations of the euro zone respected the budget targets set out in the European Union budget stability pact. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said even 50 basis points was not enough. \par \par \uc2  "The market still sees the ECB as behind the curve," said Steven Saywell, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  BEWARE THE BOJ \par \par \uc2  Some traders said yen gains this week had been triggered by Japanese investors taking profits on the recent rally in U.S. Treasuries and converting their dollar gains into yen, while others said the euro's losses across the board were the main driver for yen gains. \par \par \uc2  The dollar also came under pressure against the yen after data showed Japan had a net capital inflow of 175 billion yen in the week of October 29 compared with net outflows of more than one trillion yen in the previous week. \par \par \uc2  But verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Kuroda and from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi reminded the market Japan spent over $26 billion in September to deflect an export-damaging rise. \par \par \uc2  "There is a strong chance \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 117-118, so the risk of the dollar falling much below 120 is fairly low," said Saywell. \par \par \uc2  Analysts agreed with Japanese policy-makers that the yen's gains were not justified by fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese government said on Friday it expected the economy to shrink nearly one percent in the year to March, its worst contraction in at least 20 years, tossing out an unrealistic forecast of 1.7 percent growth. \par \par \uc2  CONSUMERS NOT CONFIDENT \par \par \uc2  Many dealers expected dollar moves to be limited by a U.S. bond market holiday on Monday. But the risks are greater for the dollar to test the downside, they said. \par \par \uc2  The market was focused on the U.S. October producer prices index at 1330 GMT, forecast to show a drop of 0.4 percent from the previous month's 0.4 percent gain, and the University of Michigan November consumer sentiment survey at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Another drop in U.S. consumer confidence was likely to pressure U.S. equities and prompt investors to unwind their dollar positions ahead of the weekend, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The University of Michigan's closely watched consumer sentiment index is expected to show a decline in confidence in November after a surprise uptick last month. Economists polled by Reuters see the index dropping to 78.7 in November from 82.7 in October. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Canadian dollar weakened beyond the key 1.60-level per U.S. dollar for the first time, on a combination of weak commodity prices and worries a deep U.S. economic slowdown will hit neighbouring Canada's economy hard. \par \par \uc2  The Canadian dollar depreciated as far as 1.6011 per dollar . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011109dxb900p5q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
