\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Euro Edges Up Vs Dlr On Position Adjustments \b0\par\par\uc2  By Audrey McAvoy \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 738 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2001\par 07:06\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The euro inched up against the dollar in Asian trade Wednesday as players covered short positions in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision on interest rates. \par \par \uc2  Amid ongoing uncertainty about the impact of the U.S.-led military campaign in Afghanistan, however, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements remained limited. \par \par \uc2  "The market isn't moving based on fundamentals, but more due to immediate supply and demand matters and keeping to a narrow range," said Noriyuki Fujita, director and head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Societe Generale Japan. \par \par \uc2  The euro's rise "is light short-covering," said a dealer at a Japanese bank. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose to a high of $0.8976 in mid-afternoon trade, up from $0.8939 in the morning session. \par \par \uc2  The dollar wasn't helped by a fall in S&P Globex Stock Index Futures, which were down at 1173.00 from 1121.00 at the New York close. Nasdaq 100 futures were at 1524.00, down from 1537.00 in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The immediate concern for many remained the outcome of the ECB's decision on interest rates Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Most economists expect the ECB to cut rates by 25 basis points given deteriorating economic conditions and receding worries about inflation. \par \par \uc2  Such a rate cut may bolster confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it would indicate it is taking steps to counter the economic downturn, and thus lift the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, said Minoru Shioiri, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Kokusai Securities, the ECB's credibility is so damaged at this point that the euro will be sold off regardless of what the bank decides Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the euro was at $0.8974, higher than $0.8948 late Tuesday in New York. The euro was at $0.8978 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y108.43, down from Y108.49 in New York late Tuesday. The euro was at Y109.17 in Tokyo late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was quoted at Y120.83, below Y121.25 late Tuesday in New York. The dollar was at Y121.60 late Tuesday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  U.S. stock futures were led lower as Qualcomm's earnings - released during U.S. after-hours trade - came in at 23 cents per share, 2 cents below analysts' consensus estimate. The issue's shares plunged 8.3% after hours. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo players expressed some skepticism towards the impact of the Qualcomm news on the dollar, however. "There was no impact on the dollar when stocks fell last week and I think this shows the connection between stocks and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  is lessening," said a German bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell against the yen, led lower by its losses against the euro. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's decline was also accelerated by stop-loss orders lined up under the Y121.00 mark that were triggered when the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell below that level, players said. \par \par \uc2  Fujita said however, that the dollar should find support at Y120.50, and others said most market players will be reluctant to sell the U.S. unit below Y120 out of fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities. \par \par \uc2  Underlining these concerns, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday said its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  totaled Y3.211 trillion in the July-September period, when it sold the yen for the dollar and the euro to stem the yen's rise in the wake of the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Ken Landon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in Tokyo, said the weighted average of MOF's dollar purchases (carried out by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was around Y117.50, making this area a crucial level for the market to watch. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.4640, up from $1.4575 in New York and higher than $1.4589 in Tokyo Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The chart of late Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates which accompanied Asia \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has\par been replaced with an enhanced \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fixture which is updated\par hourly.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Subscribers can find this table:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Telerate pages 4046 and 1087.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Dow Jones Newswires by searching the code N/IFX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Reuters by entering FRX or INT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -On Bloomberg by entering NI FRX\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011107dxb7000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
