\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Japan FX \highlight\uc2  reserves at record high on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2001\par 03:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves jumped nearly $9 billion to stand at a record high at end-October, reflecting the authorities' \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign to stem a damaging rise in the yen, the Finance Ministry said on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The nation's external reserves, already the world's largest, rose $8.686 billion from a month earlier to $405.701 billion by the end of last month. \par \par \uc2  The rise included the proceeds from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out on September 27 and 28, as \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements take place two business days after the transactions, the ministry said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven business days from September 17, mostly selling yen and buying dollars in an effort to keep the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising in the wake of the devastating terror attacks on American targets. \par \par \uc2  "There was tremendous pressure on the dollar after that incident (in the United States) and considering economic fundamentals behind the dollar and the yen, we did what we should have done," a senior ministry official said. \par \par \uc2  Reserves at the end of September had stood at $397.015 billion, up $24.798 billion from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  The ministry said it had spent 3.2107 trillion yen ($26.50 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the July-September quarter, its biggest \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a quarterly basis. \par \par \uc2  On three occasions it bought euros for yen, each time enlisting the help of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It also bought dollars for yen through the New York Federal Reserve on September 27. All \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were funded by Japan. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ, which conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the Finance Ministry's behalf, stepped into the market shortly before the dollar fell to a seven-month low of around 115.87 yen in the aftermath of the attacks on New York and Washington on September 11. \par \par \uc2  The dollar stood at 121.15/19 yen on Wednesday morning. \par \par \uc2  Out of the total reserve figure, deposits with banks headquartered in Japan, other central banks and the Bank for International Settlements fell to $69.658 billion at end-October from $77.899 billion a month earlier. \par \par \uc2  Deposits at end-September had been the highest amount since the ministry started disclosing the breakdown of where the reserves are parked in April 2000. \par \par \uc2  The official said the fall in October came as the ministry invested deposits "appropriately" as bond markets stabilised after the attacks. \par \par \uc2  ($1=121.11 Yen). \par \par \uc2      Following is a table of net \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounts during \par \par \uc2  July-September in billions of yen. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     September 17       495.5     dollar buying/yen selling\par     September 19       377.4     dollar buying/yen selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     September 21     1,287.4     dollar buying/yen selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     September 24       117.2     dollar buying/yen selling\par     September 24        21.5     euro buying/yen selling\par     September 26        94.3     dollar buying/yen selling\par     September 26        21.8     euro buying/yen selling\par     September 27       487.1     dollar buying/yen selling\par     September 27        21.9     euro buying/yen selling\par     September 28       286.6     dollar buying/yen selling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ($1=121.11 Yen).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011107dxb700591\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
