\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ's late-Sept  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen at $6.7 bln. \b0\par\par\uc2 264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2001\par 05:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 1 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ) is estimated to have spent $6.7 billion in the last two days of September to cap the yen's rise against the dollar and the euro through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , banking sources said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Data released by the BOJ showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) paid 795.7 billion yen to the private sector in October through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which mostly represents \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  As the BOJ data included the last two trading days of the previous month, it included \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 27 and 28. Traders did not detect any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in October. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on September 27 also involved enlisting the aid of the New York Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven days in September, starting shortly before the dollar fell to a seven-month low of around 115.87 yen in the wake of the attacks on New York and Washington. \par \par \uc2  By late October, it touched a 2-= month high of about 123.36 yen, encouraged by optimism over a long-term recovery in the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose from around 107 yen to a five-month peak of 111.78 yen . \par \par \uc2  The BOJ was estimated to have spent $19.40 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September up to the 26th. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as an agent for the MOF and conducts \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through transactions with brokers and commercial banks. ($1=122.45 Yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011101dxb10060v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
