\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar under pressure, market bracing for GDP. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 864 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Oktober 2001\par 08:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 31 (Reuters) - The dollar stayed under pressure on Wednesday on wariness that key U.S. third-quarter growth figures due later in the day would provide further proof of weakness in the economy, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment for the dollar deteriorated as the market shifted its focus to weak U.S. share prices and a bunch of bearish economic indicators released recently, they said. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar's fall was relatively small since there is no convincing reason to buy other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the yen and the euro, as they also have problems. \par \par \uc2  At 0642 GMT, the dollar stood at 121.80/90 yen against Tuesday's U.S. close of 121.96/2.04. \par \par \uc2  End-month commercial demand lifted the dollar to an intraday high of 122.22 yen in the morning, but the greenback slowly drifted down. \par \par \uc2  "The fall in the dollar was rather moderate despite the terrible data yesterday," said Masayuki Yamamoto, research analyst at Bank of America in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The Conference Board, a private research group, said on Tuesday its consumer confidence index tumbled 11.5 points to 85.5 in October, its lowest level in more than seven years, from a downwardly revised 97.0 in September. \par \par \uc2  "But with concerns over anthrax, uncertainty about developments in Afghanistan and extremely weak economic data, at this point, the market doesn't have much courage to buy dollars before the GDP and jobs data," Yamamoto said. \par \par \uc2  MORE U.S. DATA \par \par \uc2  The third-quarter GDP report is due at 1330 GMT. Economists polled by Reuters estimated, on average, that the economy shrank by 1.0 percent in the third quarter, which would be the worst performance in a decade. \par \par \uc2  The market may test the dollar down towards 121 yen in the near term, but no steep falls were expected amid caution over any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Japanese monetary authorities, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Masayuki Matsushima said on Wednesday there was no intention to deliberately weaken the yen but equally there was no reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise in the current climate. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials have made it clear they do not want the yen to appreciate, and so hurt exports, though the BOJ has always resisted calls to actively push it much lower. \par \par \uc2  In any case dealers doubted dollar/yen would budge much near term given talk of massive option expiries around 122.00 on Wednesday and through the week. Option positions were being defended under 121.50 and above 122.30, they added. \par \par \uc2  The euro moved little in Tokyo but edged higher from offshore lows. It may retest resistance above $0.91 in the near term, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro stood at $0.9065/70 from Tuesday's $0.9044/48. Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at 110.42/52 versus 110.36. \par \par \uc2  EXPORTING RECESSION \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also helped by the fact the United States has been all too efficient at exporting its economic woes to the rest of the world. \par \par \uc2  In export-dependent Asia, Hong Kong, Singapore, Taiwan and Japan are already in or close to recession. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday Otmar Issing, chief economist at the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conceded the euro zone faced a poor third quarter and there was no prospect of the fourth quarter being better. \par \par \uc2  Issing declined to comment on the possible outcome of the ECB policymaking council meeting next week but stressed the bank "will move quickly and powerfully when the time is right". \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the comment could help support the euro if it was taken as a hint the bank would not only cut rates next week but ease by a full 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Even the U.K., once seemingly impervious to the world slowdown, was showing symptoms of fatigue. The respected Gfk Consumer Confidence Barometer, released early Wednesday, fell by much more than expected to -5 in October from -1 the month before and a peak of +6 in June. \par \par \uc2  The survey found a marked deterioration in confidence about the U.K. economy's prospects with the expectations balance for next year diving 13 points to -33, its lowest level since September 1990. \par \par \uc2  The news kept the pound restrained at $1.4534/42 after hitting a three-week high on the dollar at $1.4600 on Tuesday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0649 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls\par                                 30 Oct.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9061   0.9044   +0.19    -4.58   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen               121.72   121.94   -0.18    +6.35   114.45\par  Euro/yen              110.28   110.30   -0.02    +1.44   108.71\par  Dlr/swiss             1.6227   1.6245   -0.11    +1.34   1.6012\par  Can/dlr               1.5789   1.5780   +0.06    +5.87   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr               0.5050   0.5041   +0.18    -9.72   0.5594\par  Euro/swiss            1.4707   1.4691   +0.11    -3.38   1.5221\par  Euro/stg              0.6232   0.6231   +0.02    -1.47   0.6325.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011031dxav00b9n\par }\page {\par