\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Economic woes depress yen, leave euro vulnerable. \b0\par\par\uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2001\par 11:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In LONDON story headlined 'Economic woes depress yen, leave euro vulnerable' please read in paragraph 13 '....Italian industrial orders data released on Monday ahowed a year-on-year decline of 3.7 percent.' \par \par \uc2  This corrects decline from 3.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  A corrected repetition follows. \par \par \uc2  (Updates prices, quotes, changes dateline, byline) \par \par \uc2  By Robin Shepherd \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 22 (Reuters) - The dollar was holding steady in a tight range against the euro on Monday with analysts focusing on Thursday's euro zone rate setting meeting, while the yen was broadly weaker on more unsettling news on the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  The latest bout of gloom on prospects for the euro kicked in on Friday with a survey showing German business confidence suffering its biggest drop for almost 28 years. That helped push the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a five-week low of $0.8965. \par \par \uc2  With the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to meet on Thursday, analysts said there was a growing feeling that monetary authorities must take decisive action or see the euro decline further. \par \par \uc2  "There's very much a short term feeling here that if the ECB doesn't cut rates either this week or in two weeks time by 50 basis points then the euro could weaken," Brendan Brown at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2  While calls are growing for the ECB to cut rates in order to stimulate its own economy, there was growing despair at the state of the Japanese economy for which monetary authorities have very little room for manoeuvre. \par \par \uc2  "The fundamental picture in Japan is looking dreadful now," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, economist at CIBC World Markets. \par \par \uc2  At 0745 GMT, the yen was down a third of a percent against the dollar. It was quoted at 121.65 yen. Against the euro, it was quoted at 109.25, down a quarter of a percent. \par \par \uc2  The euro was almost unchanged against the dollar from the New York close at $0.8995. \par \par \uc2  EURO SENTIMENT DAMPENS \par \par \uc2  The failure of the euro to firm against the dollar following the September 11 attacks and increasingly depressing economic data out of the U.S. was beginning to raise questions about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prospects in the longer term. \par \par \uc2  If the euro could not rise now, analysts reasoned, when could it ever be expected to rise? \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. economy is on the brink of recession, there's a great deal of uncertainty and you still see the dollar doing resiliantly well," said Childe-Freeman. \par \par \uc2  "So you may ask: If they are not going to sell dollars now, when are they?" she added. \par \par \uc2  To add to the bearish tone, Italian industrial orders data released on Monday showed a year-on-year decline of 3.7 percent. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN DATA \par \par \uc2  Data showing a sharp year-on-year shrinkage in Japan's trade surplus in September suggested the appearance of fallout from the September 11 attacks on the U.S. and raised more concerns about the state of the economy. \par \par \uc2  The head of the Bank of Japan's Osaka branch also said on Monday that business conditions in the region were worsening, with bank lending and fund demand dwindling. \par \par \uc2  "Economic conditions in our area are becoming severe, with exports and manufacturing slowing and capital spending, employment and incomes being hurt as a result," Takahiro Mitani told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the weakening of the yen was a product of underlying economic weakness and recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  subdued. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials do not want to see their country's export prospects further hurt by a strengthening yen. \par \par \uc2  The weak state of the world's second-biggest economy was also underscored by a decline in an index widely seen as a proxy for gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2  The Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry said its all-industries index fell 0.2 percent in August from July. \par \par \uc2  The tertiary sector index, a core component of the all-industries index mainly comprising service industries, declined 0.1 percent, METI said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011022dxam005vq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
