\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar fades against yen, stays in range. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Isabel Reynolds \par \uc2 748 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2001\par 08:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 18 (Reuters) - The dollar faded against the yen on Thursday, weighed by comments from former U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin as well as continuing concern over the effects of anthrax attacks on the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  Rubin said on Wednesday that structural reform, rather than a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was the key to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic problems. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly to pull the dollar up from a low just under 116 yen after the attacks in September. \par \par \uc2  The greenback was bid around 120.80 yen in late afternoon, having drifted from an intraday high just under 121.50. \par \par \uc2  The euro dipped briefly below 90 cents in the morning, but recovered to trade sideways, ending the afternoon around 90.34 , flat with late New York levels. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trailed to 109.28 , failing once again to hold the 110 yen level it has toyed with over the past couple of weeks. But dealers said the market seemed unwilling to push the euro much further down. \par \par \uc2  Traders took seriously the comments from Rubin, now chairman of Citigroup's executive committee, despite the fact he no longer holds a policy-making position. That is because he is a respected figure and still called upon to advise politicians, said Ron Leven, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  But Leven said the fall in U.S. stocks on Wednesday was likely to have been a more important factor in the dollar's fading vitality over the day. \par \par \uc2  U.S. VIEW UNCHANGED \par \par \uc2  Satoru Ogasawara, analyst at Credit Suisse First Boston, was also dubious of the influence of Rubin's comments, saying the message he gave on Wednesday was one often heard from the United States. \par \par \uc2  "America's stance has not changed - they tend to say a weakening yen is acceptable if structural reforms are carried out," he said. \par \par \uc2  Certainly, with the extent of the anthrax attacks still uncertain, traders were not particularly keen to dump the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and moves were limited by lacklustre trade. \par \par \uc2  "Customer business has been very light, and that has dulled activity in Tokyo trade," said a Japanese bank trader. \par \par \uc2  "Exporters especially have been hesitant to hedge because they can't establish a clear sales outlook given uncertainties about the global economy." \par \par \uc2  Solid trade may not return until the beginning of next year, said Leven of Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  "What you need is highly leveraged investors getting exciting and taking large positions. Late in what's been a very problematic year in general is not the time for that," he said. \par \par \uc2  The market largely ignored comments from Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami, who said on Thursday he could consider boosting the target for current account deposits parked at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if conditions warranted. \par \par \uc2  He steered clear of advocating other easing measures, such as inflation targeting, saying U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan was opposed to the idea. \par \par \uc2  Capital flows data released by the Finance Ministry showed Japanese investors bought a heavy net 1.0221 trillion yen ($8.43 billion) in foreign bonds in the second week of October after racking up a net 1.2391 trillion yen the week before. \par \par \uc2  Analysts, however, have said the flows were likely fully hedged, thus having a minimal impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0557 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls \par \par \uc2  17 Oct. \par \par \uc2  ----------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr              0.9026   0.9035   -0.10    -4.95   0.9496\par Dlr/yen               120.86   121.23   -0.31    +5.60   114.45\par Euro/yen              109.16   108.88   +0.26    +0.41   108.71\par Dlr/swiss             1.6369   1.6383   -0.09    +2.23   1.6012\par Stg/dlr               1.4485   1.4474   +0.08    -3.43   1.5000\par Can/dlr               1.5716   1.5704   +0.08    +5.38   1.4914\par Aus/dlr               0.5086   0.5084   +0.04    -9.08   0.5594\par Euro/swiss            1.4787   1.4803   -0.11    -2.85   1.5221\par Euro/stg              0.6229   0.6242   -0.21    -1.52   0.6325.\par \par ..        Debt...      Indicators...\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots Tokyo spots Europe spots Volatilities Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from\par BOJ World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Official rates...\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par Diaries...........        Diaries Index........\par Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters Television..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011019dxai03fb7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{