\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slips against yen, Rubin comments weigh. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 880 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2001\par 06:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 18 (Reuters) - The dollar inched lower against the yen on Thursday with fears of biological attacks on the United States continuing to gnaw at sentiment, but lacklustre trade helped it avoid a return to offshore lows. \par \par \uc2  The greenback was shoved lower mid-morning after former U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin was reported as saying it was harmful to think a weak yen would solve \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic problems. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in late September to curb an export-damaging rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , helping the dollar stay afloat in the wake of the September 11 attacks. \par \par \uc2  But despite those remarks and growing fears of an anthrax attack that closed U.S. Congress on Wednesday, the dollar managed to find support on hopes the U.S. economy would improve in the long term. \par \par \uc2  Dollar sentiment got a lift after U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Wednesday said he was confident in the long-term U.S. economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  "Rubin's comments sparked some long-dollar unwinding in an otherwise thin market for trading incentives," said a Japanese bank trader. \par \par \uc2  "But no one is really willing to trade aggressively with uncertainties over U.S. military action and the anthrax scare," he said. \par \par \uc2  By late morning, the dollar wavered at 120.95/121.00 yen from 121.23 yen in late New York and an overnight low around 120.75 yen. \par \par \uc2  The euro, which briefly slipped below 90 cents after tripping stop-loss sales, recouped at 90.32/37 cents from 90.31 cents in offshore. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at 109.24/35 yen from 108.88. \par \par \uc2  Traders suspect a prolonged threat of possible biological warfare would further depress consumer confidence and thus hurt the U.S. economy. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, U.S. stocks slumped on intensifying anthrax fears after 31 congressional staffers tested positive for exposure to the disease, forcing the closure of much of the Capitol building. \par \par \uc2  TRADING LACKLUSTRE \par \par \uc2  But with the extent of the anthrax attack still uncertain, traders were not seeing it as a major reason to dump the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and moves were limited by lacklustre trade. \par \par \uc2  "Customer business has been very light, and that has dulled activity in Tokyo trade," said another Japanese bank trader. \par \par \uc2  "Exporters especially have been hesitant to hedge because they can't establish a clear sales outlook given uncertainties about the global economy." \par \par \uc2  Top White House economic aide Lawrence Lindsey on Wednesday acknowledged what Wall Street has been saying for weeks - that the U.S. economy was likely to contract for two straight quarters, the common definition of a recession. But while the dollar sat some distance from Tuesday's high of 121.90 yen - its highest since the September 11 attacks - most expected it to be confined to a tight range. \par \par \uc2  "Downside pressure on the dollar has faded with \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and U.S. policy steps to stimulate growth," said Takashi Yamanaka, economist at Sanwa Bank. \par \par \uc2  "While there shouldn't be strong dollar buying on concerns over more terrorist attacks, there aren't strong factors to sell, either." \par \par \uc2  Japan's vice minister for international affairs told reporters on Thursday he was carefully watching \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  The yen was also seen making little headway given Japan's economic problems, with a Reuters poll on Thursday showing the economy was expected to contract by one percent this fiscal year and keep shrinking the following year. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Japan Governor Masaru Hayami said on Thursday he could consider boosting the target for current account deposits parked at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  if conditions warranted. \par \par \uc2  But he steered clear of advocating other easing measures, such as inflation targeting, saying Greenspan was opposed to the idea. \par \par \uc2  Capital flows data released by the Finance Ministry showed Japanese investors bought a heavy net 1.0221 trillion yen ($8.43 billion) in foreign bonds in the second week of October after racking up a net 1.2391 trillion yen the week before. \par \par \uc2  Analysts, however, have said the flows were likely fully hedged, thus having a minimal impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0333 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls\par                                 17 Oct.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9035   0.9035   +0.00    -4.85   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen               121.03   121.23   -0.16    +5.75   114.45\par  Euro/yen              109.36   108.88   +0.44    +0.60   108.71\par  Dlr/swiss             1.6365   1.6383   -0.11    +2.20   1.6012\par  Stg/dlr               1.4474   1.4474   +0.00    -3.51   1.5000\par  Can/dlr               1.5717   1.5704   +0.08    +5.38   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr               0.5084   0.5084   