\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar softer, anthrax scare saps trade. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 760 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Oktober 2001\par 06:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 15 (Reuters) - The dollar was a bit softer in Asian trading on Monday compared with its late New York levels in cautious trading following reports of new anthrax cases that U.S. officials linked to possible terror attacks. \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained well above its U.S. lows. \par \par \uc2  A plunge in U.S. September retail sales and news that more Americans had been exposed to anthrax sent the dollar lower in pre-weekend trade, and many Tokyo traders opted to stay on the sidelines until the situation became clearer. \par \par \uc2  By late morning the dollar was at 121.00 yen after 121.11 in pre-weekend trade, but off a low of around 120.70 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "There was a knee-jerk reaction to sell the dollar after the anthrax news, but there's still a lot of uncertainty as to what it all means," a Japanese bank dealer said. "If it means bio-terrorism, then no country is really safe," he said. \par \par \uc2  The euro was holding at 91.30/35 cents compared with 91.13 cents in late New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also well-supported against the yen, trading at 110.50/65 yen from 110.42 yen. \par \par \uc2  Making the most out of the softer dollar was the Australian dollar which spiked to one-month highs of around 51.40 cents before easing to 51.25. \par \par \uc2  The Aussie was also helped by talk on Friday that diversified miner WMC Ltd was set for a break-up or takeover by Alcoa Inc , although there have been numerous rumours involving WMC in the past 18 months. \par \par \uc2  ANTHRAX SCARE \par \par \uc2  Tokyo traders were left groping for direction after the weak U.S. economic data and new anthrax cases knocked the dollar off a fresh one-month high of 121.74 on Friday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was recouping ground lost after the September 11 attacks. \par \par \uc2  News that U.S. retail sales fell 2.4 percent in September, its steepest falloff in nearly nine-years, intensified worries that the U.S. economy was headed for recession. \par \par \uc2  "If the anthrax scare continues, then we may see additional damage to U.S. consumer spending, and that would be negative for the U.S. economy and the dollar," said Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  BOJ CAUTION LINGERS \par \par \uc2  But despite the dollar's vulnerability, traders said it would remain supported against the yen as the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities remained. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven days late last month to halt an export-damaging rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Many also doubted the dollar would see much damage as the yen struggled with problems of its own. \par \par \uc2  "The long-term trend is still for a weak yen," said Fukaya. \par \par \uc2  "There aren't many attractive investment opportunities in Japan ... and if the U.S. economy continues to slow, Japan will suffer further, too," he said. \par \par \uc2  Data on Monday showed Japan's current account surplus shrank for the ninth straight month in August. \par \par \uc2  The market also traded cautiously ahead of U.S. economic data out this week, but it was unclear how much the impact of last week's attacks would be reflected in the figures. \par \par \uc2  But some like new jobless claims and weekly chain store sales numbers will be up-to-date, describing a week falling about month after the attacks. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0349 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls\par                                 12 Oct.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9136   0.9113   +0.25    -3.79   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen               121.05   121.11   -0.05    +5.77   114.45\par  Euro/yen              110.50   110.07   +0.39    +1.65   108.71\par  Dlr/swiss             1.6208   1.6256   -0.30    +1.22   1.6012\par  Stg/dlr               1.4533   1.4526   +0.05    -3.11   1.5000\par  Can/dlr               1.5599   1.5625   -0.17    +4.59   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr               0.5123   0.5055   +1.35    -8.42   0.5594\par  Euro/swiss            1.4804   1.4815   -0.07    -2.74   1.5221\par  Euro/stg              0.6283   0.6272   +0.18    -0.66   0.6325.\par \par \par \par     ..        Debt...      Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Official rates...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Diary.......             Top events........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Diaries........... Diaries Index........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Press Digests....         Polls on G7 economies..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Reuters Television.