\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar struggles as U.S. attacks leave uncertainty. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hideyuki Sano \par \uc2 599 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2001\par 08:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 9 (Reuters) - The dollar firmed slightly against the yen on Tuesday, but remained on edge amid the uncertainty surrounding the U.S.-led military strikes on Afghanistan. \par \par \uc2  The greenback pushed up over the psychologically important 120.00 yen barrier in mid-morning, but lacked the strength to rise further in thin trade after a three-day weekend in Japan and the United States. \par \par \uc2  In mid-afternoon, it was at 119.96/01 yen up from 119.83 in London late on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was flat around 92.08/13 cents compared with 92.10 cents in early trade. It held out against the yen, bid at 110.44 yen. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trade kept to a minimum, with most dealers unable to grasp the ramifications of the latest military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including how long it would take for the U.S. to complete its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and how it would affect the economy. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the launch of retaliatory assaults by U.S. and British forces had been anticipated for so long that they barely weakened the dollar. \par \par \uc2  But many players were avoiding taking new positions, as they also see the possibility of revenge attacks on U.S. soil as very strong. A second case of anthrax diagnosed in Florida at the weekend was seen as adding to the generally nervous atmosphere. \par \par \uc2  Anthrax is a rare disease that experts say can be used as a biological warfare agent. \par \par \uc2  "There is fear of other terror attacks on the U.S. If that happens, the dollar could dive," said Yasuji Yamanaka, deputy general manager at Nikko Trust and Banking. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the dollar is still below where it was both against the yen and the euro before the U.S. attacks on Afghanistan took place seems to suggest the market does have such a worry," Yamanaka added. \par \par \uc2  Market players were also eager to see how U.S. equities would perform later on Tuesday. Stocks slipped only slightly on Monday after the first round of attacks, but trade was extremely thin due to the Columbus Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  ALONE ON \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  "It remains difficult for the dollar to rise unless U.S. equities rise, so people are looking to the euro and temporarily to the Swiss franc," said Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  The yen has limited room to rise, with the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  still looming at the lower ends, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "If there are speculative dollar sales, Japanese authorities will no doubt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Yamanaka of Nikko Trust. Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said Japan had not made a decision yet as to whether further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was needed after the attacks, but added there may be a need if speculative moves destabilise the market. \par \par \uc2  The meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers at the last weekend agreed that decisions on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be left up to individual countries, he added. \par \par \uc2  "There will be no coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... But we are seeing a situation where there is a chance for speculative moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Countries need to watch their own markets and make their own efforts for stability," Shiokawa said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  seven days last month in an effort to protect Japanese exporters by preventing the yen from soaring out of control. \par \par \uc2  "At least this means he has effectively got authorisation from other countries for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so that will help keep the dollar firm," said Tokyo-Mitsubishi's Fukaya. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011010dxa900dqo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
