\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  moves dampened by c.banks deeds, investor doubt. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Charlotte Cooper \par \uc2 844 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2001\par 17:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 8 (Reuters) - Central banks' presence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since September 11, both directly and by quiet persuasion, has helped dampen potential volatility but now investors' own indecision is acting as a brake, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  While there has been heightened fluctuation in the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the attacks on the United States, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility has not hit extremes. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's biggest reaction to the attacks on September 11 was against the Swiss franc and the yen, falling five percent to 20-month lows on the franc and seven-month lows against the yen. \par \par \uc2  It recovered four percent on both in subsequent weeks and has so far shed a relatively mild one percent in reaction to Sunday's strikes by the United States and Britain on Afghanistan. \par \par \uc2  Analysts on Monday said central banks' liquidity boosting actions in the immediate aftermath of the attacks, rounds of interest rate cuts and direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like days of yen selling by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , have contributed to a reasonably orderly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market response to the shocks on the global financial system. \par \par \uc2  "It is right to say the perception that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to provide liquidity has reduced the war premium on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatilities," said Michael Metcalfe, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Credit Agricole Indosuez. \par \par \uc2  For Avinash Persaud, global head of research for State Street, there had been the direct \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action, like the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "But they've also been on the sidelines whispering 'Don't take out too much risk'." \par \par \uc2  While the "whispering" may continue, its impact was likely to be lessened as markets recovered. "There's tremendous uncertainty limiting market activity. Portfolio investors are not running out there strongly convinced what to do," he said. \par \par \uc2  "Speculators will be emboldened with time. But it's not clear whether the uncertainty will clear with time - it's still not clear where you should put your money." \par \par \uc2  SURPRISING ORDERLINESS \par \par \uc2  In the days after the attacks the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided billions in liquidity to calm markets; they, the Bank of Japan and the Swiss National Bank all cut interest rates to stimulate growth and, the case of the SNB, to stem export-damaging appreciation of the franc. \par \par \uc2  Implied volatility reflects expectations of future \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fluctuations and three-month options volatilities on dollar/yen reached 12.5-14.0 percent just after the disaster. They now stand at 10.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  By contrast, analysts say dollar/yen volatilities screamed above 20 percent in the wake of the Russian crisis in 1998 and sometimes hit 15 percent at the end of Japan's fiscal year. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit a six-month low against the euro on September 17 and three-month euro/dollar volatility peaked at a close of 13.87 a day later, compared with 11.75 before the attacks. \par \par \uc2  Neil MacKinnon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Merrill Lynch, said the orderly response partly reflected central banks' readiness to step in if they considered markets moving away from fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  "But it partly reflects the fact that \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  investors cut back positions and are unwilling to take on big bets. That's a function of the increased risk aversion and uncertainty at the present time," he said. \par \par \uc2  "MORAL SUASION" \par \par \uc2  For Persaud, some potential poison had been drawn because crossborder investors had not had huge positions to unwind before the attacks on New York and Washington. \par \par \uc2  But central banks also exerted some "moral suasion" in the days after the disaster when the markets were uncertain whether the payments' system would hold up. \par \par \uc2  "If you are uncertain whether the payments system will hold up, you need central banks. They say 'If you are going to need me, I'm not going to help you out if you are putting on risky bets'." \par \par \uc2  Some analysts agree central banks leaned implicitly on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the immediate aftermath through the liquidity they provided to soothe payment system concerns. \par \par \uc2  "Investment banks were very reluctant to do anything other than the minimum," said one who declined to be named. \par \par \uc2  "But over the last two weeks people have been swinging the bat in a very major way and I don't think whatever central banks may want to achieve has really had a big effect on people." \par \par \uc2  However for Tony Norfield, ABN Amro's head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research, there was no implicit pressure. \par \par \uc2  "There wasn't a gentleman's agreement. It was more real uncertainty about the implications of these events." \par \par \uc2  "On dollar/yen, you know the downside is protected by the Bank of Japan and the upside is limited by the risk of repatriation and other things." \par \par \uc2  Russell Jones, Lehman Brothers, said while historically volatility could have been expected to have been greater, there was still scope ahead for large \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  "It depends on how events play out...If there was a major political event in Saudi Arabia or Pakistan or Israel, I'm not sure how successful any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy can be," he said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011008dxa800th5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
