\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slips on safe-haven flows, mkt wary of BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Natsuko Waki \par \uc2 681 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2001\par 09:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The dollar slipped against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday as risk-averse investors shifted their funds to safe-haven assets such as the Swiss franc following the U.S.-led strikes on Afghanistan. \par \par \uc2  But dollar falls against the yen were limited by the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to restrain the export-damaging strength of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "People knew some retaliation was going to happen, so we are at the expected stage. There are a number of questions at the next stage as to what is going to happen and that is generating some uncertainty in the market," Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers, said. \par \par \uc2  "But against the yen, the BOJ have indicated they are pretty resolved to act against yen strength and such jitters have, to some degree, helped the dollar." \par \par \uc2  U.S. and British forces launched strikes on Afghanistan on Sunday in the first military response to the air attacks on September 11 on New York and Washington. President Bush vowed military action would go on until those suspected of the attacks on the United States were driven into the open. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said trading was muted with Japan and the U.S. markets closed for holiday, exaggerating price movements. They noted a drop in U.S. equity futures meant the dollar would struggle further when markets reopen on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  By 0742 GMT, the dollar was at the day's lows around 119.61 yen, nearly a yen lower compared with the New York close of 120.50 on Friday. But dealers said this was a tame reaction compared with the fall of over two yen suffered on September 11. \par \par \uc2  The main gainer on the day was the Swiss franc, rising one percent against the dollar to 1.6014 francs from the New York close of 1.6162 on Friday. But gains were still limited compared with its surge to 1.6340 from 1.6880 on September 11. \par \par \uc2  The euro erased earlier losses against the dollar, gaining a half a percent to $0.9231 from $0.9183 in late New York trade on Friday. The euro was a shade softer on the yen at 110.49 from 110.62. \par \par \uc2  Dealers suspected already risk-averse Japanese investors would become even more so now hostilities had begun. That reduced speculation Japanese institutions would send more of their massive funds offshore in search of higher yields at the start of the new fiscal half-year which began this month. \par \par \uc2  BEWARE OF BOJ \par \par \uc2  Traders were reluctant to push the yen too far, having been left in no doubt about the Japanese authorities' resistance to such a move after a month of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Last month the BOJ bought at least $20 billion, and perhaps nearer $30 billion, restraining the yen following its rise to seven-month highs around 115.75 in the wake of the attacks. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is doing okay for now but we never know what's going to happen. But what we all know is that the BOJ is determined. So we need to be very careful especially below 120 and 119 yen," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  In the last round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late September the BOJ asked its counterparts in the euro zone and United States to sell yen on its behalf. \par \par \uc2  "They can of course \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or the Fed if the want, whenever they want," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, there was as yet no sign any other member of the Group of Seven industrialised nations was prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own account. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the G7 did not discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at their meeting over the weekend, though the communique did say the group would continue to monitor exchange markets closely and cooperate as appropriate. \par \par \uc2  The main thrust of the communique was that the group stands united to track down and intercept assets of terrorists and to pursue individuals and countries suspected of financing them. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011008dxa800ffw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
