\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar struggles as investors seek safer shores. \b0\par\par\uc2 817 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2001\par 07:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Oct 8 (Reuters) - The dollar struggled to regain \par \par \uc2  its balance against the yen and Swiss franc after a knee-jerk \par \par \uc2  fall following the U.S.-led strikes on Afghanistan. \par \par \uc2      Still, the dollar managed to skirt further losses as \par \par \uc2  players opted for the sidelines to watch the developments of \par \par \uc2  the U.S. military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  "Enduring Freedom". \par \par \uc2      Dealers said the strikes, which are the first military \par \par \uc2  response to the September 11 attacks, were hardly unexpected. \par \par \uc2      But caution gripped the market as the conflict looked like \par \par \uc2  being a drawn out affair with the U.S. emphasising there was no \par \par \uc2  magic bullet to end it quickly while their chief target, Osama \par \par \uc2  bin Laden, vowed there would be no peace for America. \par \par \uc2  With Japanese markets on holiday, the dollar's fall was \par \par \uc2  largely a mark-down by traders reluctant to deal in any \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid such uncertainty. Treasuries and some futures \par \par \uc2  contracts are also closed, further starving the market of \par \par \uc2  direction. \par \par \uc2  Overall, dealers expected a moderate resurgence in global \par \par \uc2  risk aversion to benefit the Swiss franc and the yen, though \par \par \uc2  the euro was missing out this time in part because the market \par \par \uc2  was reconsidering hopes for a euro zone rate cut this week. \par \par \uc2  "The military response was always a question of when not \par \par \uc2  if, so from that perspective the market impact will be muted," \par \par \uc2  said Mike Moran, an economist at Standard Chartered in Hong \par \par \uc2  Kong. \par \par \uc2  "The Swiss and yen are likely to benefit, while the dollar \par \par \uc2  softens a little bit. And as uncertainty creeps in again, a lot \par \par \uc2  of emerging market-related \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will likely feel the \par \par \uc2  heat," he added. \par \par \uc2  Moran singled out those from Australia, New Zealand, South \par \par \uc2  Africa and some in Asia, particularly the Indonesian rupiah \par \par \uc2  which tumbled more than a 1,000 rupiah to 10-week lows on \par \par \uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2  By early afternoon in Asia, the dollar had slipped to \par \par \uc2  119.85 yen from 120.50 in New York late on Friday, a staid \par \par \uc2  reaction compared to the fall of over two yen suffered on \par \par \uc2  September 11. \par \par \uc2  Similarly, while it eased to 1.6108 Swiss francs from \par \par \uc2  1.6162, that was positively restrained compared to the plunge \par \par \uc2  from 1.6880 to 1.6340 seen on the day of the attacks. \par \par \uc2  The euro was conspicuous by its failure to rally, instead \par \par \uc2  sitting quietly at $0.9188 hardly changed from New York's late \par \par \uc2  $0.9183. \par \par \uc2  That was partly due to selling against the yen, which \par \par \uc2  dragged it to 110.17 yen from 110.62, with traders suspecting \par \par \uc2  that already risk-averse Japanese investors would become even \par \par \uc2  more so now hostilities had begun. \par \par \uc2  That in turn dealt a blow to speculation that Japanese \par \par \uc2  institutions would send more of their massive funds offshore in \par \par \uc2  search of higher yields. \par \par \uc2  BEWARE OF BOJ \par \par \uc2  On the other hand, traders were reluctant to push the yen \par \par \uc2  too far having been left in no doubt about the Japanese \par \par \uc2  authorities' resistance to such a move after a month of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market is not panicking, but there is nervousness. \par \par \uc2  Uncertainties on how long this military action would last and \par \par \uc2  how this would affect the U.S. economy should make the dollar \par \par \uc2  vulnerable," said a senior dealer at a Japanese bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  "But any major speculative dollar sales would be limited \par \par \uc2  due to caution over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . I think the \par \par \uc2  BOJ is ready anytime should the dollar lose ground again," he \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ bought at least $20 billion last month, and perhaps \par \par \uc2  nearer $30 billion, restraining the yen following its rise to \par \par \uc2  seven-month highs around 115.75 in the wake of the attacks. \par \par \uc2  And just because Monday was a holiday in Japan did not mean \par \par \uc2  the bank could not ask its counterparts in the euro zone and \par \par \uc2  United States to sell yen on its behalf, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, there was as yet no sign that any other \par \par \uc2  member of the Group of Seven industrialised nations was \par \par \uc2  prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own account. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said the G7 did \par \par \uc2  not discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at their meeting over the weekend, \par \par \uc2  though the communique did say the group would continue to \par \par \uc2  monitor exchange markets closely and cooperate as appropriate. \par \par \uc2  The main thrust of the communique was the group stands \par \par \uc2  united to track down and intercept assets of terrorists and to \par \par \uc2  pursue individuals and countries suspected of financing \par \par \uc2  terrorists. \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg did appear \par \par \uc2  to try to cool speculation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was about to cut \par \par \uc2  interest rates at its policy meeting on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "At the current juncture the level of key ECB interest \par \par \uc2  rates is seen to be consistent with maintaining price stability \par \par \uc2  over the medium term," Duisenberg told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was a lot more concerned about the \par \par \uc2  economic outlook than Duisenberg and would be disappointed if \par \par \uc2  the bank did not ease this week, perhaps taking it out on the \par \par \uc2  euro. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011008dxa8006bu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
