\par\par \b \uc2  O'Neill, Shiokawa Agree To Cooperate On Global Economy \b0\par\par\uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Oktober 2001\par 22:12\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa and U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill agreed to cooperate to help the global economy emerge from its slump, a Japanese Finance Ministry official said Saturday. \par \par \uc2  Meeting ahead of a gathering of Group of Seven finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors, O'Neill and Shiokawa affirmed the importance of working together toward maintaining economic growth and market confidence. \par \par \uc2  O'Neill told Shiokawa that he was "well aware" of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the yen's surge in the wake of the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks in the U.S., the official said. \par \par \uc2  "Treasury Secretary O'Neill expressed understanding of Shiokawa's explanation," the official said. \par \par \uc2  The two sides didn't discuss the possibility of taking joint action in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and O'Neill didn't mention the U.S. policy on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Japanese official said. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  last month after the dollar plunged in the wake of the U.S. terrorist attacks. In a series of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  estimated to have topped $20 billion, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  hoisted the dollar back above Y120 from a Y115.80 low it hit shortly after the assaults. \par \par \uc2  The aggressive action by Japanese authorities put a lid on the yen's rise, which threatened to hurt Japan's already stumbling economy by stifling exports and exacerbating deflation. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa told reporters earlier this week that he didn't plan to seek coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from other G7 countries to curb the yen's strength. \par \par \uc2  However, Japan was widely expected to seek at least a nod of approval from the U.S. regarding its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market steps. By securing O'Neill's "understanding," Japanese authorities likely accomplished a key objective in Washington. \par \par \uc2  Briefing Shiokawa on recent developments in the U.S., O'Neill said U.S. authorities were taking measures to support the economy, explaining the Federal Reserve's interest rate cuts and the government's fiscal pump-priming measures, which include tax cuts and increased spending. \par \par \uc2  O'Neill told Shiokawa that the attacks had damped economic activity, but that he expected U.S. growth to pick up in the middle of next year, according to the Japanese official. \par \par \uc2  Explaining the situation in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Shiokawa told O'Neill that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was providing ample liquidity to ease conditions in financial markets. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa also told O'Neill that Japan's government was pressing ahead with efforts to clean up the banking sector, and planned to use the Resolution and Collection Corp. to help banks offload their bad loans, according to the official. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Shiokawa and O'Neill also agreed to cooperate to disrupt terrorist\par financing, a major theme of Saturday's G7 meeting.\par    -By Arran Scott, Dow Jones Newswires; 1-240-888-0753;\par arran.scott@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dxa609zzh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
