\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED -  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar holds fire ahead of U.S. jobs data. \b0\par\par\uc2 692 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2001\par 12:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      In LONDON story headlined "\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -Dollar holds fire ahead of \par \par \uc2   U.S. jobs data" please read in 15th paragraph...reach parity by \par \par \uc2   the end of the year 2002....instead of...reach parity by the end \par \par \uc2   of the year...(making clear forecast is for 2002 not 2001). \par \par \uc2  (Updates prices, adds fresh quotes, comments from ECB's Liebscher, France's Fabius, changes byline) \par \par \uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 5 (Reuters) - The dollar was steady on Friday in muted trade ahead of key U.S. jobless data later in the session, with traders on the alert for further signs the U.S. economy may be heading for recession. \par \par \uc2  Employment data for September are due at 1230 GMT and are forecast to show a fall in non-farm payrolls of 109,000, following a drop of 113,000 in the previous month. \par \par \uc2  Data on Thursday showed weekly U.S. unemployment claims surged to their highest level in nine years, rekindling fears the United States may tip into recession after last month's suicide attacks. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone is on hold ahead of the U.S. payrolls," said Francesca Fornasari, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  "Poor weekly jobless claims numbers yesterday have raised concern of a disappointing payroll number and this is weighing on the dollar at the margins." \par \par \uc2  Weekly U.S. jobless claims soared to 528,000 in the week ended September 29. \par \par \uc2  German industrial orders data are due at 1000 GMT and are forecast to show a month-on-month rise of 0.1 percent in August, and a year-on-year fall of 5.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The euro traded in a range of less than half a cent against the dollar, and was quoted near the bottom of that range at $0.9166/68 at 0930 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 120.50 yen , in the middle of its one-third of a yen range. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a weekend meeting of the Group of Seven finance ministers and a long weekend in both Japan and the United States were also keeping volumes to a minimum. \par \par \uc2  "We could see a closing out of some positions ahead of the G7 meeting and the holidays on Monday, although markets are no longer expecting any kind of G7 statement on the yen," said Kamal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Friday that concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be a topic of discussion with U.S. Treasury Secretary Paul O'Neill at their bilateral meeting this weekend. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the second half of September to curb an export-damaging rise in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "On \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we have been acting on our own judgment, not on a coordinated basis," Shiokawa told reporters. \par \par \uc2  EURO RATE OUTLOOK \par \par \uc2  Analysts said they were becoming increasingly optimistic for the euro against the dollar, with Commerzbank forecasting the euro would reach parity by the end of the year 2002 (corrects). \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  council member Klaus Liebscher said current interest rates in the euro zone were compatible with its goal of ensuring stable prices in the medium term, saying last month's 50 basis point cut in rates did not represent any softening of the ECB's commitment to its primary goal of price stability. \par \par \uc2  French Finance Minister Laurent Fabius told the International Herald Tribune he hoped for lower European interest rates to tackle the prospect of slowing growth, but ruled out altering the euro zone's stability pact to stimulate the economy. \par \par \uc2  SWISS FRANC STAGES BRIEF GAINS \par \par \uc2  A report that Russian authorities were investigating Thursday's explosion of Russian passenger plane flying over the Black Sea as a terrorist act weighed briefly on the dollar and gave the safe haven Swiss franc a short-lived boost. \par \par \uc2  News of the Russian airliner crash, coming after the suicide plane attacks on U.S. cities last month, was seen heightening risk aversion. \par \par \uc2  "The Russian airliner news was a reminder of the negatives surrounding the dollar these days and in that sense, European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are most likely to benefit," one bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011005dxa500gl7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
