\par\par \b \uc2  Asia Markets-Investors eye Philippine gloom. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Nick Edwards \par \uc2 1,234 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2001\par 12:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      HONG KONG, Oct 5 (Reuters) - Investors ignored tame \par \par \uc2  inflation data in the Philippines on Friday, eyeing instead \par \par \uc2  weak economic fundamentals that left Manila's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \par \par \uc2  stock markets stuck in ruts and sank its third biggest listed \par \par \uc2  firm to nine year lows. \par \par \uc2      Only local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds bounced on news that Philippine \par \par \uc2  inflation had slowed to 6.1 percent year on year in September \par \par \uc2  from 6.3 percent in August, opening the window for more \par \par \uc2  interest rate cuts after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lopped 25 basis \par \par \uc2  points off key rates on Thursday. \par \par \uc2      But a 10 basis point drop in peso Treasury bill yields was \par \par \uc2  not enough to convince equity investors that the economy was on \par \par \uc2  the mend and the key Philippine Composite Index ended down 0.6 \par \par \uc2  percent, closing the week 3.4 percent lower than it started. \par \par \uc2      Foreign brokerages sold a net 10.76 million pesos \par \par \uc2  ($208,000) worth of Philippine shares on Friday, placing sell \par \par \uc2  orders worth a total of 220.68 million pesos and buy orders \par \par \uc2  totalling 209.92 million pesos. Turnover reached 535.26 million \par \par \uc2  pesos against Thursday's 426.77 million. \par \par \uc2      Index heavyweight Philippine Long Distance Telephone Co \par \par \uc2  fell to its lowest in almost nine years to close at 410 pesos \par \par \uc2  and led the decliners. \par \par \uc2      PLDT lost 2.38 percent as its debt financing concerns \par \par \uc2  continued to weigh on market sentiment. The stock has fallen \par \par \uc2  24.77 percent since the September 11 attacks on the United \par \par \uc2  States which prompted it to postpone a planned $250 million \par \par \uc2  bond issue. \par \par \uc2      Investors are negative on Manila's ability to kick start \par \par \uc2  its flagging economy with its policy options severely limited \par \par \uc2  by a massive public debt burden. \par \par \uc2      The amount of new fiscal stimulus required by many of the \par \par \uc2  region's flagging economies is not seen as sustainable by \par \par \uc2  investors who are already nervous about existing debt \par \par \uc2  positions. \par \par \uc2      "Many of the economies in Asia are restrained by huge \par \par \uc2  public debt, for example the Philippines and Indonesia have \par \par \uc2  public debt almost the size of their GDP," Keon Lee, deputy \par \par \uc2  head of Asia Pacific economic and policy research at JPMorgan \par \par \uc2  told Reuters Television. \par \par \uc2      "Thailand is another economy where investors are looking \par \par \uc2  carefully at the budget. There's not a lot of room for fiscal \par \par \uc2  expansion," he said. JPMorgan is forecasting emerging Asia \par \par \uc2  growth to slow to almost zero this year from around seven \par \par \uc2  percent in 2000 with a pick up to between two and 2.5 percent \par \par \uc2  in 2002, Lee said. \par \par \uc2      YEN LOCKED IN RANGE \par \par \uc2      Japan's external reserves rose by $24.798 billion to a \par \par \uc2  record $397.02 billion in September, boosted mainly by \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as authorities \par \par \uc2  fretted that an overvalued yen was hurting exports. \par \par \uc2      It was the biggest monthly rise in reserves on record, not \par \par \uc2  counting technical adjustments. \par \par \uc2      Analysts said the figure was in line with expectations and \par \par \uc2  fitted in with market estimates that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent \par \par \uc2  about $19.4 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  up to late September. \par \par \uc2      In recent months, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves -- the largest in the \par \par \uc2  world -- have been rising by about $4-5 billion a month. \par \par \uc2      The dollar loitered in a tight range on Friday as market \par \par \uc2  players kept moves to a minimum ahead of the release of a U.S. \par \par \uc2  jobs report later in the day and a weekend meeting of Group of \par \par \uc2  Seven (G7) finance ministers. \par \par \uc2      A three-day weekend ahead in both Japan and the United \par \par \uc2  States also sapped volume. \par \par \uc2      The dollar was stuck around 120.54/58 yen in late Tokyo \par \par \uc2  from 120.45/55 yen in late U.S. trade, with the dollar \par \par \uc2  supported by yen-selling against the euro dealers said. \par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE DOLLAR SINKS \par \par \uc2      The Singapore dollar was knocked to its knees in late trade \par \par \uc2  as dollar buy orders from London caught the market short and \par \par \uc2  pushed it to 1.7845, the lowest level since August 7. \par \par \uc2      The Sing dollar was hobbled by wariness ahead of the \par \par \uc2  government's announcement of its flash estimate for third \par \par \uc2  quarter gross domestic product growth due next week, with many \par \par \uc2  expecting a negative outcome. \par \par \uc2      Full year GDP is also expected to be lowered as the \par \par \uc2  city-state has been hard hit by the electronics downturn. \par \par \uc2      TAIWAN BUCKS FLAT FRIDAY \par \par \uc2      Asian equity markets ended the week narrowly mixed with \par \par \uc2  benchmark indices basically flat on Friday, with Taiwan's TAIEX \par \par \uc2  bucking the market trend to gain 2.6 percent. \par \par \uc2      Investors chased technology issues after Dell Computer \par \par \uc2  announced surprisingly positive news, but analysts warned that \par \par \uc2  the rally could be short-lived. \par \par \uc2      The main TAIEX index extending Thursday's 1.38 percent \par \par \uc2  rise, inspired by an aggressive easing of domestic monetary \par \par \uc2  policy. \par \par \uc2      Despite the two-day rally, The TAIEX, which hit a near \par \par \uc2  nine-year low on Wednesday, has still shed 16.4 percent since \par \par \uc2  the September 11 attacks in the United States. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors were net buyers of T$3.05 billion (US$88 \par \par \uc2  million) in shares listed on Taiwan's main stock exchange on \par \par \uc2  Friday, bringing total net buying to T$5.55 billion over the \par \par \uc2  past two sessions. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo's Nikkei 225 benchmark gained just 0.39 points, Hong \par \par \uc2  Kong's Hang Seng lost 0.09 percent, South Korea's KOSPI gained \par \par \uc2  around a quarter of one percent and Singapore's Straits Times \par \par \uc2  Index added 0.56 percent. \par \par \uc2  The smaller markets of the Philippines, Indonesia, Thailand \par \par \uc2  and Malaysia marked similarly small moves. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. $0924 GMT \par \par \uc2  Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.49       120.60         +0.09\par  Sing dlr      1.7842       1.7802         -0.22\par  Taiwan dlr     34.51        34.53         +0.06\par  Korean won   1311.00      1312.00         +0.08\par  Baht           44.69        44.63         -0.12\par  Peso           51.55        51.52         -0.06\par  Rupiah       9830.00      9725.00         -1.07\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.