\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen under pressure, dlr awaits Fed decision. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Dhara Ranasinghe \par \uc2 676 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Oktober 2001\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 2 (Reuters) - The yen shed a third of a percent against the dollar and euro on Tuesday as Japan reiterated its determination to keep the yen down and Japanese investors returned to foreign assets after end-September book-closing. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, meanwhile, was steady against the euro ahead of the U.S. Federal Reserve's interest rate decision around 1815 GMT. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely tipped to cut rates 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  The yen's losses down to fresh three-week lows against the dollar and six-week troughs versus the euro came after Japan's finance minster said he was ready to act if the dollar fell again. \par \par \uc2  "The Bank of Japan through its aggressive action has helped weaken the yen," said Tom Vosa, market economist at National Australia Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Japanese investors were also raising their exposure to overseas assets, having repatriated foreign funds in recent weeks to bolster their balance sheets ahead of the financial half-year end. \par \par \uc2  At 1152 GMT, the yen stood around 120.50 per dollar, having fallen more than half a percent to lows near 121 earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the yen stood near six-week lows around 110.80. \par \par \uc2  FOMC TAKES CENTRE STAGE \par \par \uc2  The dollar was little changed around $0.9175 per euro, with markets keenly awaiting the U.S. Federal Reserve Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting later in the day. \par \par \uc2  Of the 25 primary dealers of U.S. government securities surveyed by Reuters last week, 21 forecast the Fed to lower its key rate half a point to 2.50 percent, with four expecting a quarter point cut. \par \par \uc2  The Fed last lowered rates on September 17 in the wake of the attacks on New York and Washington, cutting the fed funds rate by 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  "Markets are expecting a 50 basis point cut and if this is delivered, it should be dollar supportive," said Mitul Kotecha, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Credit Agricole Indosuez in London. \par \par \uc2  "The sharp sell-off in the dollar in the aftermath of the (September 11) attacks seems to have been pared back a bit." \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Fed may also signal its willingness to ease monetary policy further, a move which could boost stock markets and, with them, the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Prospects for the U.S. economy looked better on Monday after the National Association of Purchasing Management's (NAPM) monthly index showed slightly better-than-expected results. \par \par \uc2  The NAPM said its monthly index slipped to 47.0 in September after a jump to a nine-month peak of 47.9 in August, but beating the market's consensus estimate of 45.5. \par \par \uc2  YEN ON DEFENSIVE \par \par \uc2  The yen was held down as comments from Japanese officials keept markets alert to the prospect of further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said earlier he was ready to act if the dollar fell again, while Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi said it was important that \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets should reflect fundamentals. "Probably, the only reason the dollar is up here is that the Bank of Japan (BOJ) has pushed it there," said Steve Barrow, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bear Stearns in London. \par \par \uc2  "Also, the key for me is whether at the start of the second half of the fiscal year we'll see an end to some of the repatriation flows into the yen." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least seven occasions since September 17 to weaken the yen to help its exporters. \par \par \uc2  Focus was also back on Japan's frail economy after the tankan survey of business sentiment on Monday showed corporate confidence slumped in September for a third straight quarter, adding to bearish yen sentiment. \par \par \uc2  "It is no coincidence that the yen's move follows an extremely weak tankan survey," said Credit Agricole's Kotecha. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone unemployment and economic sentiment data had no major impact on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. The August jobless rate came in slightly better than expected at 8.3 percent. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dxa206hi0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
