\par\par \b \uc2  "Mr. Yen" Says Global Recession Imminent - Kyodo \b0\par\par\uc2 559 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2001\par 10:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- Global recession is imminent as the U.S. economy may enter a recession in the wake of the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks on New York and Washington, and the U.S. economy is unlikely to recover until April-June 2002 at the earliest, former top Finance Ministry bureaucrat Eisuke Sakakibara told Kyodo News in a recent interview. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. economy is heading for a recession, with its growth in the July-September and October-December quarters likely falling into negative territory," said Sakakibara, who teaches at Keio University. \par \par \uc2  "The downturn in the U.S. economy would have serious effects on the Japanese economy as well as the global economy, and the world is highly likely to simultaneously enter a recession," he said. \par \par \uc2  The former vice finance minister in charge of international affairs told Kyodo News that U.S. share prices have not yet hit bottom, while U.S. firms will report decreases in earnings and personal consumption in the country will be sluggish. \par \par \uc2  "The issue is when an economic recovery (in the U.S.) will take place, and the most optimistic view is that the economy would start to recover in the April-June quarter next year," said Sakakibara, dubbed "Mr. Yen" while he was a vice finance minister because of his aggressive market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the current situation allows U.S. authorities to take additional monetary and fiscal policies such as further rate cuts and tax breaks, adding the effectiveness of such measures will be a prerequisite for an early recovery. \par \par \uc2  At the moment, there are no signs of a rebound in share prices, he said, adding they might rebound during April-June if an economic recovery becomes apparent. \par \par \uc2  The Sept. 11 terror attacks shocked the world, and confidence in the U.S. economy has been damaged substantially. Equity plunges in the U.S. have spread to other countries and the dollar has slid against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities have been conducting dollar-buying, yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest the yen's rise as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  thinks a weak yen is desirable for an early economic recovery in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "I think the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are right, and I hope (authorities) will do so until they win," Sakakibara said, adding current \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not pose any problem for U.S. authorities. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. feels that the exchange rate of Y125-Y130 to the dollar is acceptable, but will be concerned if Japan intentionally tries to bring the level to Y140-Y150," Kyodo quoted him as saying. \par \par \uc2  He also said the current U.S. administration does not like the idea of conducting market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it might have to do so if the dollar takes a nosedive. \par \par \uc2  Remarking on a meeting of finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors from the Group of Seven leading industrialized countries to be held next Saturday, Sakakibara said measures to block the flow of funds to international terrorists will be the top item on the agenda. \par \par \uc2  The G7 top financial officials will discuss measures to supplement the U.S. administration's defense and national security policies, he said. \par \par \uc2  He told Kyodo News that restricting the flow of funds is the "right" and "desirable" move to fight terrorism, but it may have negative effects on the global economy by shrinking international financial transactions \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011001dxa1000fe\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
