\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Confirms  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  To Sell Yen Just Now \b0\par\par\uc2 119 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2001\par 13:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  yet again on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the second time in Friday's global session, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official confirmed Friday. \par \par \uc2  "We took appropriate action on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets," the official said, after the dollar jumped some 60 sen to near Y119.40. \par \par \uc2  The official would not comment, however, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted through the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa confirmed an earlier round of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the MOF ordered the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to buy dollars for\par yen early Friday in Tokyo.\par   -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010928dx9s000qz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
