\par\par \b \uc2  Japan MOF Mizoguchi: Yen Still Too Strong \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2001\par 02:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The head of the International Bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Friday the yen is still too strong and the ministry will continue to take steps in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to counter the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  "The yen is still excessively strong, and we will respond flexibly and take appropriate action in the market," Zembei Mizoguchi told a group of reporters at the ministry. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi spoke after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen lifted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a high of 120.05 overnight. \par \par \uc2  At 0010 GMT Friday, the dollar was trading at Y119.65. \par \par \uc2  "We have continued to say the same thing. Since August the yen has risen, largely on speculation, and not as a reflection of Japan's economic conditions," Mizoguchi said. \par \par \uc2  "Watching the market, we decided we needed to fix the situation, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to an excessive rise by the yen in the market," he added. \par \par \uc2  Asked if having the U.S. Federal Reserve \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's behalf overnight indicated an increased level of international cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mizoguchi would only say, "we are in regular contact with authorities from other countries." \par \par \uc2  So far, in the series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has conducted since the terrorist attacks in the U.S., it has acted on its own and not in conjunction with other Group of Seven nations. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -By Audrey McAvoy, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par audrey.mcavoy@dowjones.com\par -0- 28/09/01 00-33G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010928dx9s0000f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
