\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen stuck near lows after BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chisa Fujioka \par \uc2 810 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2001\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Sept 28 (Reuters) - The yen was pinned near two-week lows against the dollar on Friday after Japanese monetary authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the seventh day in the past two weeks. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest action to restrain the yen followed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday which Japanese officials said involved enlisting the aid of both the New York Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The dollar seems supported at 119 yen for now after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today, but there's still pressure on the dollar given pessimism over the U.S. economy," a Japanese bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hovered at 119.23/29 yen in late Tokyo trade having jumped more than a half-yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a low of 118.95 following the local commercial fix. That compares with a late offshore level of 119.66. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said the dollar already faced pressure after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as speculators, who had predicted BOJ action, sold on rallies. Exporters were also keen to sell on any dollar uptick. \par \par \uc2  The yen pared its losses against the euro, with the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed by exporter sales at 108.92/07 yen from 109.81 in late New York. It was off a one-month peak at 110.22 yen in overnight trade. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro eased to 91.46/51 cents from 91.79. \par \par \uc2  BOJ HAND \par \par \uc2  Dealers saw no end to the BOJ's latest yen-selling campaign, which started as the dollar fell to near seven-month lows around 115.75 yen last week after suicide aircraft attacks on U.S. cities raised chances the world's biggest economy would tip into recession. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, confirming Tokyo had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said economic fundamentals warranted a slightly weaker yen and that Tokyo was determined to combat speculative moves to push up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities are seen keen to stamp out a yen rise which hurts Japanese exporters' earnings, a factor that has weighed on Tokyo's Nikkei share average. \par \par \uc2  Japan has also been suspected of using a weaker yen as a means to ward off deflationary pressures on the economy, though analysts said the theory looked ill-placed given near-zero interest rates and the flood of liquidity already in the market. \par \par \uc2  And while some saw the BOJ easing its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign after the fiscal half-year book-closing on Friday, most said that was unlikely. \par \par \uc2  Although a weaker yen helped companies window-dress books, a mere one-time fix held little meaning in a market working under mark-to-market principles. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar-selling pressure should continue as the flow out of U.S. assets doesn't seem to be easing yet," said Koji Fukaya, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "It's unlikely that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will stop after the end of the fiscal half-year, when the dollar looks set to start falling again," he said. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN DATA \par \par \uc2  The market reacted little to a set of dour economic data from Japan, with dealers saying the yen already reflected the grim state of the economy. \par \par \uc2  Japan posted on Friday a worse-than-expected rise in August industrial production, but the news hardly caused a ripple in the market. \par \par \uc2  Data also showed Japan's unemployment rate stuck at a record high 5.0 percent in August, while consumer prices slid for the 23rd straight month. \par \par \uc2  The market instead chose to focus on U.S. data overnight which showed the number of Americans claiming unemployment benefits rose to a nine-year high of 450,000 last week. \par \par \uc2  With economists saying it was probably too early to assess the full impact of the aircraft attacks on the United States on jobs, the U.S. economic outlook remained shrouded in uncertainty. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0616 GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                        Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2000 Cls\par                                 27 Sep.\par                        -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr              0.9147   0.9181   -0.37    -3.68   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen               119.18   119.70   -0.43    +4.13   114.45\par  Euro/yen              109.13   109.86   -0.66    +0.39   108.71\par  Stg/dlr               1.4696   1.4739   -0.29    -2.03   1.5000\par  Can/dlr               1.5785   1.5775   +0.06    +5.84   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr               0.4921   0.4876   +0.92   -12.03   0.5594\par  Euro/swiss            1.4782   1.4797   -0.10    -2.88   1.5221\par  Euro/stg              0.6220   0.6222   -0.03    -1.66   0.6325.\par \par \par \par     ..        Debt...      Indicators...\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reports..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f2